# Markdown is deliberately NOT formatted by prettier.
#
# `docs/*` and the root README are **public-facing and take two sign-offs, never one**
# (DEV-PROTOCOL §3), and reflowing them would produce a large diff in documents whose review is about
# their claims. A formatter is a code-style gate; it has no business rewriting a sentence that three
# people agreed on.
*.md

# scripts/verify-environment.ts is DEV2's file inside DEV3's tree (DEV-PROTOCOL §3's carve-out).
# Reformatting it would be editing another developer's file to satisfy a gate they never agreed to,
# so it is excluded until DEV2 says otherwise — it is one `prettier --write` away from being included
# and that is DEV2's call, not mine.
scripts/verify-environment.ts

# The generated vector corpus. Two hundred machine-written files, rebuilt on demand and never
# committed (see .gitignore), so there is nothing for a formatter to keep tidy — and checking them
# would put a slow, always-changing set in front of a gate whose value is that it is fast and
# stable. The four hand-written vectors beside them ARE checked.
test-vectors/generated/

# packages/bindings/src is MACHINE OUTPUT and is byte-compared against a fresh generation
# (scripts/generate-bindings.ts). Formatting it to our rules would make it permanently "drifted":
# the check would fail on every run, for a difference nobody introduced, and the fix a reader would
# reach for is to stop running the check. The generator's formatting is part of the artefact.
packages/bindings/src/
